# ArtesaNFC — Cloudflare Pages static routing.
#
# Private certificate route (/c/{token}): an unbounded token space that cannot
# be pre-rendered as one static folder per token. This rewrite serves the
# single certificate shell for any /c/* request; the shell extracts the token
# from the URL path client-side (hydrate-certificate.js) and validates the
# route shape there.
/c/*  /c/  200

# Public detail routes (F-08): /piezas/{slug} and /artesanos/{slug} are served
# by ONE neutral shell per entity type, kept under /_shell/ (outside the
# /piezas/ and /artesanos/ namespaces, so no slug can collide with it). The
# shells carry no entity content: hydrate-detail.js reads the slug from
# location.pathname and shows the entity only after the public API answers 200,
# so the API is the sole authority on publication. There is deliberately no
# per-slug static page.
#
# Why `:slug` and not `*` (verified on Wrangler 4.135.0, docs/QA_PRIVATE_ROUTE.md
# section 5): the first matching rule wins and a 200 rewrite applies even over
# an existing file. `/piezas/*` also matches `/piezas/` (empty splat) and would
# replace the list page with the shell. `:slug` is exactly one non-empty
# segment: it never matches `/piezas/` or a nested path. A rule without a
# trailing slash does not match the path with one (and vice versa), so both
# forms are listed. The lists `/piezas/` and `/artesanos/` have no rewrite;
# nested paths such as /piezas/a/b/ keep their previous behaviour.
/piezas/:slug  /_shell/pieza/  200
/piezas/:slug/  /_shell/pieza/  200
/artesanos/:slug  /_shell/artesano/  200
/artesanos/:slug/  /_shell/artesano/  200
